WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.210
“Free coins, and every level unlocked!”

2
00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:05.650
That’s what a modded game

3
00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:07.010
promised one of my students.

4
00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:10.950
A week later, his phone was full of

5
00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:13.790
pop-ups and his data bundle had vanished.

6
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.740
Free turned out to be expensive.

7
00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:21.190
Today: how malware gets onto phones and

8
00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:23.670
computers, and how you keep it out.

9
00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:27.340
Malware means malicious software:

10
00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.080
any program made to harm a device

11
00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:31.540
or the person using it.

12
00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:34.510
It can steal your passwords, watch what

13
00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:37.370
you type, flood you with adverts, or

14
00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.270
lock your files and demand money.

15
00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:42.090
There are a few main kinds.

16
00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:45.390
A virus hides in a file and

17
00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:46.930
spreads when it’s shared.

18
00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:50.190
A worm spreads by itself across a network.

19
00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:52.960
A trojan pretends to be useful,

20
00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:54.760
like a free game hack.

21
00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:57.340
Ransomware locks your files

22
00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:58.480
and demands payment.

23
00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:01.690
Spyware quietly watches what you do.

24
00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:04.960
Surprisingly, most malware

25
00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:06.180
doesn’t break in.

26
00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:07.500
It’s invited.

27
00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:10.840
Modded apps and cracked games from

28
00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:12.360
outside the official store.

29
00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:15.110
A USB stick passed around

30
00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:16.110
at the cyber café.

31
00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:18.630
An attachment you weren’t expecting.

32
00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:21.600
And fake alerts that shout, “Your

33
00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:23.140
phone has three viruses!”

34
00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.620
It’s like a stranger at your door

35
00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:28.500
with a beautiful gift box.

36
00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:31.540
Malware rarely smashes a window:

37
00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.520
usually, you carry the box in yourself.

38
00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:37.230
That’s why one kind is named

39
00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.650
after the Trojan horse.

40
00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:40.610
Quick check!

41
00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.820
A website suddenly says my phone

42
00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:46.660
has three viruses and tells me to

43
00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:48.440
install a cleaner now.

44
00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:50.350
What should I do?

45
00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:52.190
Close the page.

46
00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:54.870
A website can’t look inside your phone,

47
00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:58.170
so the alert is fake, and the “cleaner”

48
00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:00.010
is often the malware itself.

49
00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:02.440
If you’re worried, open your

50
00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:04.120
phone’s own protection yourself.

51
00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:08.130
Now the defences, and why they work.

52
00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:11.330
Updates close the holes malware uses.

53
00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:13.860
Official stores check apps

54
00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:14.780
before you get them.

55
00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:16.960
Built-in protection scans

56
00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:17.760
what you install.

57
00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:19.990
And a backup means even

58
00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:21.610
ransomware can’t take your work.

59
00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:23.760
How would you know?

60
00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:27.180
The battery drains much faster than usual.

61
00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:29.560
Adverts pop up everywhere.

62
00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:31.990
There’s an app you don’t

63
00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:32.770
remember installing.

64
00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.220
Or your data bundle vanishes overnight.

65
00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:38.940
Think a device is infected?

66
00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:41.380
Turn off Wi-Fi and mobile

67
00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:42.760
data, so it can’t spread.

68
00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:46.320
Tell your IT teacher or an adult at home.

69
00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:48.540
Change important passwords

70
00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:49.900
on a clean device.

71
00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:52.640
Then remove the app, or

72
00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:53.800
restore from a backup.

73
00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:55.850
Your turn.

74
00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:58.810
Your cousin offers you a cracked copy

75
00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:01.190
of a paid game on a USB stick.

76
00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:04.120
It’s free, and it’s from family.

77
00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:05.740
Do you install it?

78
00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:09.710
No: cracked games are one of the easiest

79
00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:12.330
ways in for malware, even from family.

80
00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:15.770
Remember: apps only from the official

81
00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:18.810
store, everything updated, a backup

82
00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:21.030
kept, and if something feels wrong,

83
00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:22.930
disconnect and tell someone.

84
00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:26.440
Try it tomorrow: open your phone’s

85
00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:28.420
settings and check two things.

86
00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:30.380
Are automatic updates on?

87
00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:33.120
And is there an app you don’t recognise?

88
00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:36.560
On a shared family phone, ask an

89
00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:38.480
adult before you remove anything.
